diff --git a/docs/roadmap/agent-core-memory-observatory-shadow-mode-implementation-plan.md b/docs/roadmap/agent-core-memory-observatory-shadow-mode-implementation-plan.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4f6356c51c2597aea8a83f6d6d3b97304e936213
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/roadmap/agent-core-memory-observatory-shadow-mode-implementation-plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,1618 @@
+# Agent Core Memory Observatory + Shadow-Mode Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` (recommended) or `superpowers:executing-plans` to implement this plan task-by-task. Every implementation task uses RED → GREEN → regression → verification → commit → push → remote readback.
+
+**Goal:** Build a loopback-only, real-time Memory Observatory at `http://127.0.0.1:3697` that visualizes Agent Core memory nodes/typed edges on the left and a live activity/trace tracker on the right, while keeping the new memory system in shadow/canary validation until real-time correctness, recovery, and performance are proven stable.
+
+**Architecture:** Agent Core DMF remains the sole memory authority. Memory and operational activity is emitted through a best-effort observer sink into the existing tamper-evident AuditJournal; persisted audit sequence numbers become the replayable real-time event cursor. A read-only Memory Observatory projection exposes bounded graph snapshots and node details through exact-loopback internal endpoints. A separate local sidecar serves a React/Vite UI on port `3697` and proxies only read-only observatory endpoints; killing the UI/server must never stop memory, MCP, execution, or Codespace work.
+
+**Tech Stack:** TypeScript 7, Node.js 24 built-in HTTP/SSE, SQLite/FTS5 through existing DMF, existing AuditJournal + correlation system, React 19 + Vite 8 in a separate subproject, `@xyflow/react` for graph interaction, Vitest, Testing Library, Playwright for browser acceptance. No external AI/model/API dependency.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/roadmap/agent-core-cross-session-memory-nervous-system-design.md` sections 35–37 and Phase 8, extended by the approved Shadow-Mode requirement from the September 1, 2026 discussion: do not replace the current live Codespace path until the Observatory proves real-time memory behavior stable.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- DMF remains the only semantic memory authority; no second SQLite/vector/LangGraph memory authority.
+- The Observatory is observer-only and has zero mutation authority.
+- Default Observatory host is exactly `127.0.0.1`; default UI port is `3697`.
+- Port `3697` must not be made public by Codespace lifecycle scripts. If browser access needs Codespaces forwarding, visibility remains private.
+- The current live Codespace connector/runtime is not replaced merely because the UI works.
+- Initial runtime mode is `shadow`; hard lifecycle enforcement is not escalated by this plan until the explicit canary/cutover gates are satisfied.
+- Existing shared-memory endpoints, Memory Context Lease, cognition controller, remote hydration, and remote durability remain authoritative and are extended, not duplicated.
+- Existing AuditJournal remains the durable activity flight recorder. Do not create a second durable activity database.
+- Activity streaming is best-effort and must never block a successful memory mutation, tool call, execution run, or HTTP response.
+- A dropped live-stream event must be detectable by sequence gap and recoverable from persisted AuditJournal records when retained.
+- If retained audit history is no longer available, the UI must show an explicit historical gap and refresh from an authoritative graph snapshot; never fabricate missing activity.
+- Activity records expose only safe IDs, bounded metadata, reason codes, statuses, relative workspace paths where allowed, and redacted text. Never expose API keys, OAuth tokens, Memory Remote encryption keys, leases, raw secrets, hidden reasoning, or principal identifiers.
+- The UI never accepts a principal identifier from the browser. Agent Core resolves the stable memory principal internally and binds requests to one configured workspace/project scope.
+- Graph snapshots are bounded. Starting defaults: 500 nodes, 2,000 edges, 250 recent activities. Hard maxima: 1,000 nodes, 5,000 edges, 2,000 recent activities.
+- Existing memory performance target remains `100k active memories: preflight p95 < 150 ms`.
+- Observatory instrumentation may add at most 10% relative p95 overhead to the existing 100k preflight benchmark and must still remain under 150 ms.
+- Local persisted-event → browser-visible activity target: p95 < 250 ms.
+- Authoritative memory mutation → graph convergence in browser target: p95 < 500 ms.
+- Cross-project contamination = 0; cross-principal contamination = 0.
+- Unjustified new-node acceptance = 0; required linked-node orphan rate = 0.
+- `.vscode/`, secrets, stable tunnel identity/defaults, and unrelated work are not touched.
+- No force-push. Every green checkpoint is pushed and read back from GitHub before moving to the next task.
+- No live cutover is performed by this plan's documentation task; implementation ends at a verified cutover-ready gate unless the user explicitly authorizes replacement.
+
+---
+
+# 1. Target Runtime Topology
+
+```text
+                         EXISTING AUTHORITY
+
+ChatGPT / Codespace tools
+          │
+          ▼
+   Agent Core Runtime
+          │
+          ├──────────────► DMF / Continuity / Remote Durability
+          │                       AUTHORITATIVE
+          │
+          ├──────────────► AuditJournal
+          │                 persisted ordered activity
+          │                       │
+          │                       ├── recent replay
+          │                       └── live persisted-record stream
+          │
+          └──────────────► Read-only Observatory Projection
+                                  │
+                                  ▼
+                      exact-loopback internal API
+                                  │
+                                  ▼
+                 Memory Observatory sidecar process
+                      127.0.0.1:3697
+                                  │
+                  ┌───────────────┴──────────────┐
+                  ▼                              ▼
+          LEFT: MEMORY GRAPH             RIGHT: LIVE ACTIVITY
+          nodes + typed edges            trace / tracker / log
+```
+
+Critical failure-isolation invariant:
+
+```text
+kill Memory Observatory UI/server
+            ↓
+Agent Core memory still works
+Codespace MCP still works
+execution still works
+remote durability still works
+```
+
+## 1.1 Truthful capture boundary
+
+During isolated shadow testing, the Observatory can only display activity that actually passes through the shadow Agent Core / candidate MCP path. It must not pretend to observe ChatGPT/Codespace operations that bypass that path.
+
+```text
+current live connector operation
+  bypasses shadow candidate
+        ↓
+NOT PRESENT in shadow activity tracker
+```
+
+```text
+shadow/canary MCP operation
+  passes through candidate Agent Core
+        ↓
+PRESENT in tracker + memory graph
+```
+
+Do not compensate for this boundary with filesystem polling that guesses user/agent intent. Real-work visibility begins in the advisory canary stage when work is deliberately routed through the candidate path, and becomes complete for that path only after controlled cutover.
+
+---
+
+# 2. UI Contract
+
+The first stable layout is intentionally close to the approved reference:
+
+```text
+┌───────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┐
+│ MEMORY GRAPH / NODE CARDS                 │ LIVE ACTIVITY             │
+│                                           │                           │
+│  [A3 Failure] ─resolved_by─► [A4 Solution]│ 11:24:03 preflight.start  │
+│                              │            │ 11:24:04 recalled A4      │
+│                         validated_by      │ 11:24:04 remember_more    │
+│                              ▼            │ 11:24:05 read file        │
+│                         [A5 Validated]     │ 11:24:09 test.failed      │
+│                                           │ 11:24:18 revision.created │
+│                                           │ 11:24:19 remote.synced    │
+├───────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┤
+│ NODE INSPECTOR / FILTERS / CONTEXT        │ EVENT DETAILS / FILTERS   │
+└───────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+Starting desktop proportions:
+
+```text
+left graph workspace   68%
+right tracker          32%
+minimum right width    360 px
+```
+
+The UI must remain usable down to 1024 px viewport width. Below that width the activity tracker becomes a collapsible right drawer; the graph remains primary.
+
+## 2.1 Node card minimum fields
+
+```text
+title
+memory kind
+state
+current revision number
+root / branch indicator
+bounded current-value preview
+last updated timestamp
+last recalled indicator
+write-decision badge when available
+remote durability badge at scope level
+```
+
+The title uses `memory_node_metadata.title` when available and falls back to the canonical key. The browser never invents a title using AI.
+
+## 2.2 Edge families
+
+Primary semantic edges render with labels:
+
+```text
+continues
+supersedes
+branch_of
+derived_from
+learned_from
+caused_by
+failed_because
+resolved_by
+validated_by
+blocked_by
+depends_on
+produced
+contradicts
+```
+
+Associative edges remain visually secondary:
+
+```text
+same_anchor
+same_artifact
+same_route_or_task
+same_task_family
+cooccurs_in_event
+token_overlap
+temporal_neighbor
+```
+
+The client never infers a new edge. Every line originates from authoritative `memory_edges` data.
+
+## 2.3 Real-time visual states
+
+```text
+RECALLED          node pulse/highlight
+REMEMBER_MORE     source + expanded path highlighted
+NODE_CREATED      node appears after authoritative snapshot refresh
+REVISION_CREATED  revision badge increments
+EDGE_CREATED      new authoritative edge appears
+CONFLICT_OPENED   conflict marker becomes visible
+REMOTE_PENDING    durability badge shows pending
+REMOTE_SYNCED     durability badge shows synced
+STREAM_GAP        tracker warning + graph snapshot resync
+```
+
+Animations are finite and informational. No infinite decorative motion.
+
+---
+
+# 3. Read-only API Contract
+
+The internal Agent Core API remains on the Agent Core loopback service port. The sidecar on `3697` proxies these endpoints so the browser never needs direct cross-origin access to port `8765`.
+
+Proposed exact-loopback routes:
+
+```text
+GET /internal/memory-observatory/health
+GET /internal/memory-observatory/snapshot
+GET /internal/memory-observatory/node/:memoryId
+GET /internal/memory-observatory/activity?after=<sequence>&limit=<n>
+GET /internal/memory-observatory/stream
+```
+
+The sidecar exposes browser-facing read-only routes:
+
+```text
+GET /api/health
+GET /api/snapshot
+GET /api/node/:memoryId
+GET /api/activity
+GET /api/stream
+```
+
+No `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, or `DELETE` browser route is permitted in v1.
+
+## 3.1 Snapshot interface
+
+```ts
+export interface MemoryObservatorySnapshot {
+  schemaVersion: 1;
+  generatedAt: string;
+  auditSequence: number;
+  project: {
+    projectId: string;
+    workspaceLabel: string;
+  };
+  status: {
+    memoryHealthy: boolean;
+    lifecycleMode: 'disabled' | 'advisory' | 'enforce';
+    remoteEnabled: boolean;
+    remoteDurabilityState: string;
+    hydrationState?: string;
+    generationId?: string;
+    logicalStateHash?: string;
+  };
+  nodes: MemoryObservatoryNode[];
+  edges: MemoryObservatoryEdge[];
+  conflicts: MemoryObservatoryConflict[];
+  continuity: MemoryObservatoryContinuitySummary;
+  truncated: {
+    nodes: boolean;
+    edges: boolean;
+  };
+}
+```
+
+## 3.2 Node interface
+
+```ts
+export interface MemoryObservatoryNode {
+  memoryId: string;
+  title: string;
+  canonicalKey: string;
+  kind: MemoryKind;
+  state: MemoryState;
+  revisionNo: number;
+  valuePreview: string;
+  importance: number;
+  pinned: boolean;
+  rootReason?: string;
+  branchParentMemoryId?: string;
+  createdFromDecisionId?: string;
+  createdAt: number;
+  updatedAt: number;
+}
+```
+
+No `principalId` field is permitted in the projection.
+
+## 3.3 Edge interface
+
+```ts
+export interface MemoryObservatoryEdge {
+  edgeId: string;
+  fromMemoryId: string;
+  toMemoryId: string;
+  relation: MemoryRelation;
+  weight: number;
+  evidenceEventId?: string;
+}
+```
+
+`edgeId` is deterministically derived from `fromMemoryId + relation + toMemoryId`, not from random browser state.
+
+## 3.4 Activity interface
+
+```ts
+export interface MemoryObservatoryActivity {
+  sequence: number;
+  timestamp: string;
+  category: 'memory' | 'continuity' | 'tool' | 'execution' | 'routing' | 'remote' | 'http' | 'system';
+  event: string;
+  state?: 'started' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'pending';
+  requestId?: string;
+  traceId?: string;
+  routeContextId?: string;
+  toolName?: string;
+  runId?: string;
+  executionNodeId?: string;
+  memoryIds?: string[];
+  relation?: MemoryRelation;
+  decisionType?: MemoryPersistenceDecisionType;
+  reasonCodes?: string[];
+  statusCode?: string;
+  durationMs?: number;
+}
+```
+
+The activity projector uses a whitelist. It must not pass arbitrary `AuditJournalRecord.data` to the browser.
+
+---
+
+# 4. File Structure
+
