+# 12. Definition of Stable
+
+The Memory Observatory + memory candidate may be called stable only when:
+
+```text
+1. Real memory operations create the expected visible node/revision/edge outcome.
+2. `remember_more` highlights only persisted bounded expansion history.
+3. Every new non-root node has a justified semantic edge.
+4. Every new root exposes its persisted fresh-context reason.
+5. Failure history survives solution/validation.
+6. Browser refresh/restart reproduces the authoritative graph.
+7. SSE disconnect/reconnect neither duplicates nor silently loses retained events.
+8. Audit retention gaps are explicit.
+9. UI crash has zero effect on memory/execution/MCP correctness.
+10. Cross-Codespace deletion/recovery reproduces identical logical memory state.
+11. Remote durability state is truthful in the UI.
+12. Scope isolation remains zero-contamination.
+13. No secret/lease/principal leakage is present.
+14. Existing 100k preflight p95 remains <150 ms.
+15. Observatory overhead and real-time latency meet this plan's gates.
+16. Full Agent Core/Codespace release regression remains green on the exact remote-visible SHA.
+```
+
+Only then may the project advance to controlled live integration.
